{%- comment -%} Vitals Product Information block (carved from the v9 single-file section). {%- endcomment -%}
{%- comment -%}
  CON-3354: the H1/H2 tag select is gone — the heading is always an h2
  (the safe-coexistence default the old setting shipped with; themes keep
  their own h1). The text itself is now a merchant-editable inline
  richtext defaulting to the product title dynamic source, with size /
  color / weight / per-device margins driven from block settings.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- liquid
  # Fall back to the live product title when the setting is blank OR when
  # the stored default is the UNRESOLVED dynamic-source literal (same
  # hardening as the description-tabs default). The literal is built at
  # runtime so this file's own source never contains it.
  assign vtls_lb = '{' | append: '{'
  assign title_content = block.settings.title
  if title_content == blank or title_content contains vtls_lb
    assign title_content = product.title | escape
  endif
-%}
{%- comment -%}
  Injector discoverability (same pattern as the quantity/picker
  blocks): Vitals places widgets relative to the product title
  via the ProductTitle document injector, whose selector list is
  matched by priority. `product__title` on the wrapper matches the
  high-priority `.product__title > h1` selector, and the
  `title`-bearing class on the heading matches `h1/h2[class*="title"]`
  — both far above the bare-heading catch-alls.
{%- endcomment -%}
<div class="vtls-pi__title product__title Vtls-{{ block.id }}" {{ block.shopify_attributes }}>
  <h2 class="vtls-pi__title-text">{{ title_content }}</h2>
</div>
{%- comment -%}
  KEEP THIS {% style %} BELOW THE MARKUP. `{% style %}` renders an inline
  <style> element as a real child of the `.shopify-block` wrapper that
  `content_for` puts around every block, so with the style tag first the
  title is never the wrapper's first child and the `> * + *` owl below
  would match the title itself — an 8px phantom gap on every render, with
  no widget injected, that also outranks this block's own margin-top
  settings (the owl carries an id, the setting rules two classes). The
  Details group documents the same hazard: it spaces its children with a
  flex row-gap precisely because inline <style> tags emitted by child
  blocks would create phantom gaps under a margin owl. Emitting the style
  tag last keeps the title the genuine first child; the owl then matches
  only the trailing <style> (display:none, so the margin has no effect)
  until a widget is actually injected.
{%- endcomment -%}
{% style %}
  .vtls-pi__title.Vtls-{{ block.id }} {
    margin-top: {{ block.settings.margin_top }}px;
    margin-bottom: {{ block.settings.margin_bottom }}px;
  }
  .Vtls-{{ block.id }} .vtls-pi__title-text {
    margin: 0;
    font-size: {{ block.settings.title_size }}px;
    color: {{ block.settings.title_color }};
    font-weight: {% if block.settings.title_style == 'regular' %}400{% else %}700{% endif %};
  }
  @media screen and (max-width: 749px) {
    .vtls-pi__title.Vtls-{{ block.id }} {
      margin-top: {{ block.settings.margin_top_mobile }}px;
      margin-bottom: {{ block.settings.margin_bottom_mobile }}px;
    }
    .Vtls-{{ block.id }} .vtls-pi__title-text {
      font-size: {{ block.settings.title_size_mobile }}px;
    }
  }
  {%- comment -%}
    Spacing for widgets Vitals injects next to the title (the Product
    Reviews stars snippet is the common one). The injector always zeroes
    the ANCHOR's margin on the side facing the snippet — inline
    `margin-bottom: 0` when it inserts below, inline `margin-top: 0` when
    it inserts above — so the gap can only ever live on the INJECTED
    node: an inline style beats any rule this file can write. That is
    also where a theme's gap comes from on a theme page (Horizon: 8px on
    the injected node). Our section has no such rule, and its 20px stack
    gap can't reach the node either: `content_for` wraps each block in
    `.shopify-block`, so the snippet always lands one level below
    `.vtls-pi__info`, either beside the heading or beside this wrapper
    depending on which selector the ProductTitle injector matches. Cover
    both anchors AND both placements, matching Horizon's 8px:
      - below the title — the snippet is the TRAILING sibling, so the
        owl's margin-top lands on the snippet itself. Correct as-is.
      - above the title — the snippet is the LEADING sibling, so the owl
        would target our own title, whose inline margin-top the injector
        has just set to 0 (the margin would silently do nothing). Mirror
        the rule with `:has(+ <title>)` so the margin-bottom lands on the
        snippet instead.
    Each placement therefore puts a real margin on exactly one node — the
    injected one — so the two rules can never stack into a 16px gap, and
    neither can override this block's own margin_top/margin_bottom
    settings. See the comment above the tag for why this <style> element
    has to stay below the markup.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  #vtls-pi-{{ section.id }} .vtls-pi__title.Vtls-{{ block.id }} > * + *,
  #vtls-pi-{{ section.id }} .shopify-block:has(> .vtls-pi__title.Vtls-{{ block.id }}) > * + * {
    margin-top: 8px;
  }
  #vtls-pi-{{ section.id }} .vtls-pi__title.Vtls-{{ block.id }} > *:has(+ .vtls-pi__title-text),
  #vtls-pi-{{ section.id }} .shopify-block:has(> .vtls-pi__title.Vtls-{{ block.id }}) > *:has(+ .vtls-pi__title.Vtls-{{ block.id }}) {
    margin-bottom: 8px;
  }
{% endstyle %}

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "Product title",
  "settings": [
    {
      "type": "header",
      "content": "Appearance"
    },
    {
      "type": "inline_richtext",
      "id": "title",
      "label": "Title",
      "default": "{{ product.title }}"
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "title_size",
      "label": "Title size (desktop)",
      "min": 10,
      "max": 64,
      "step": 1,
      "unit": "px",
      "default": 32
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "title_size_mobile",
      "label": "Title size (mobile)",
      "min": 10,
      "max": 64,
      "step": 1,
      "unit": "px",
      "default": 28
    },
    {
      "type": "color",
      "id": "title_color",
      "label": "Title color",
      "default": "#222222"
    },
    {
      "type": "select",
      "id": "title_style",
      "label": "Title style",
      "options": [
        {
          "value": "regular",
          "label": "Regular"
        },
        {
          "value": "bold",
          "label": "Bold"
        }
      ],
      "default": "bold"
    },
    {
      "type": "header",
      "content": "Spacing"
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "margin_top",
      "label": "Top margin (desktop)",
      "min": 0,
      "max": 100,
      "step": 1,
      "unit": "px",
      "default": 0
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "margin_bottom",
      "label": "Bottom margin (desktop)",
      "min": 0,
      "max": 100,
      "step": 1,
      "unit": "px",
      "default": 0
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "margin_top_mobile",
      "label": "Top margin (mobile)",
      "min": 0,
      "max": 100,
      "step": 1,
      "unit": "px",
      "default": 0
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "margin_bottom_mobile",
      "label": "Bottom margin (mobile)",
      "min": 0,
      "max": 100,
      "step": 1,
      "unit": "px",
      "default": 0
    }
  ],
  "presets": [
    {
      "name": "Product title"
    }
  ]
}
{% endschema %}
